  "summary": "The released 1.1.0 portable app brings the recovery-observability review into a source-bound downloadable bundle: compare onboard transitions with received confirmation, then export the same evidence shown in the UI.",
  "rationale": "The original deterministic C++ executive and Python replay oracle remain intact. Versioned archives, native-safe POSIX packaging and an extracted-executable Chromium journey make the new received-witness feature reviewable beyond a source checkout. An independent boot/reset oracle and downloaded JSON comparison prevent a static page or source-service fallback from passing acceptance.",
  "limitations": [
    "Educational software-only executive; no flight hardware, operational SAFE assertion or mission qualification.",
    "Unsigned portable folder, not an installer or clean-machine installation proof. Exact-source three-OS builds and asset digests require publication review.",
    "Unsigned desktop portable folders, not system installers or clean-machine proof. Three-OS extracted-native checks drive an owned URL; default OS browser opening remains manual."
